      "lightVolume": "./models/ava-barbat.light.gz?v=98aa66c8b3",
      "statement": [
        "My proposal reimagines the Ann Arbor Farmers Market as a place where circulation becomes an opportunity for connection. Organized around a central circulation space and terrace, the building brings visitors together while encouraging movement between market activities, gathering spaces, and different levels.",
        "The experience begins outside, where the canopy extends the market into the site and creates a sheltered approach. Visitors move from the surrounding streets through outdoor market spaces toward the building’s shared center. Rather than treating circulation as a passage between destinations, the design makes it a social space where people can pause, meet, and observe the activity around them.",
        "The central terrace anchors this experience, providing a gathering place that connects indoor and outdoor life. It offers space to sit, eat, and spend time together while maintaining a visual relationship with the market below. Connections between levels encourage visitors to explore and encounter different activities throughout the building.",
        "Concrete structure establishes a consistent rhythm, while openings and skylights bring daylight into the interior. Together, these decisions support a market that feels connected, welcoming, and active. The proposal creates a shared destination where everyday movement supports spontaneous encounters and strengthens the market’s role as a place for community."
      ]
    }
